From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:42:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] northbridge/intel/haswell: Refuse DIMMs with more than 10
 column bits

Haswell Trad only addresses DDR3 devices with 10 column address bits.
MAD_DIMM tells the controller the size, ranks and width of a DIMM, not
its column bits, so a 16 GiB SO-DIMM of 8 Gb x8 devices (11 column
bits) is mapped wrongly. Ticket 626 shows what happens with the native
RAM init: the margins look fine, the machine boots with mangled
graphics, memtest86+ crashes and the OS hangs. Neither the OEM firmware
nor mrc.bin supports such DIMMs. The memory test of the native RAM init
goes through the controller and cannot see the column bit that the
controller never drives, so nothing stops the boot today.

Leave such a DIMM out, with an error that names its slot, and go on with
the others. Stopping instead (die()) beeps and flashes the LEDs on these
boards (H8_BEEP_ON_DEATH, H8_FLASH_LEDS_ON_DEATH), but the reason stays
in the pre-RAM console, which nothing can read on a W541: it has no
serial port and CBMEM never comes up. With the DIMM left out the laptop
boots with less memory and the reason is in cbmem -1. The error is
printed when the SPDs are read and once more after cbmem_recovery(): a
DIMM change forces a training, and the log of a training overflows the
16 KiB pre-RAM console, which keeps only its end, so the first line
would be lost on exactly the first boot with such a DIMM.

The DIMM's decoded data is cleared, so it does not add to the channel
size and configure_mc.c does not pick it as DIMM A; with the previous
commit SMBIOS then lists the DIMMs that remain, in their own slots. Its
ranks leave the rank map, so the JEDEC init, the training and MAD_DIMM
skip them. That is not quite an empty slot: the module stays on the bus
and loads its lines, its mode registers are never written, and the CADB
writes of the other ranks' mode registers set CKE for all four ranks
(reut.c, cke = 0xf). The training runs with the module in place, so the
margins include it, but nobody has run such a setup yet: the hardware
test below covers it. If the other DIMMs do not train with it in place,
the boot stops after the second attempt, as before. When no DIMM is
left, return RAMINIT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED_MEMORY with its own message
rather than "No DIMMs were found".

A fast boot compares the DIMM records with the cached ones. They are the
same on every boot, so the cache keeps working, and a DIMM change still
forces a training. ULT builds keep accepting every DIMM: the ticket
names Haswell Trad only. The check is in the shared northbridge and
applies to the T440p as well, which has the same limit.

TEST=Host syntax check with -Werror and the ci-150 W541 nri config. Host
unit test of collect_spd_info() and report_ignored_dimms() with
synthetic DDR3L-1600 SO-DIMM SPDs (8 GiB of 4 Gb x8 devices, 16 GiB of
8 Gb x8 devices) decoded by spd_decode_ddr3(): four 8 GiB DIMMs
unchanged and nothing to repeat; one 16 GiB DIMM in CH0S0 left out
(rank map 0xc, 8 GiB on channel 0, slot 1 is DIMM A) and repeated; both
DIMMs of channel 1 left out (channel 0 only); four 16 GiB DIMMs return
UNSUPPORTED_MEMORY; no DIMM still returns NO_MEMORY_INSTALLED, and a
new SPD pass forgets the DIMMs left out before. The same test fails on
the code before this change. Still to test on the W541 (nri): with the
four 8 GiB DIMMs no "DIMM ignored" line and 32 GiB as before. With a 16
GiB DIMM, if one is at hand: the laptop boots on the others; cbmem -1
of that first, training boot has the error after the start of the CBMEM
console; dmidecode -t 17 lists the remaining DIMMs in their slots and
not the 16 GiB one; with the module left in place, 30 minutes of
stress-ng --vm 4 --verify (or a memtest86+ pass) find no error, and
ddr-report shows margins close to those of the same DIMMs without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c   |  2 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h   |  1 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/spd_bitmunching.c  | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
index af784fbc9d..019606ebad 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
@@ -210,6 +210,8 @@ void perform_raminit(const bool s3resume)
 		system_reset();
 	}
 
+	report_ignored_dimms();
+
 	/* Save training data on non-S3 resumes */
 	if (!s3resume)
 		save_mrc_data();
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
index 1d45bb8fe2..487389eea0 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h
@@ -617,6 +617,7 @@ void raminit_main(enum raminit_boot_mode bootmode);
 void raminit_reset(void);
 
 enum raminit_status collect_spd_info(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
+void report_ignored_dimms(void);
 enum raminit_status initialise_mpll(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
 enum raminit_status convert_timings(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
 enum raminit_status configure_mc(struct sysinfo *ctrl);
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/spd_bitmunching.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/spd_bitmunching.c
index a481ad80ad..f051564445 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/spd_bitmunching.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/spd_bitmunching.c
@@ -74,6 +74,51 @@ static void decode_spd(struct raminit_dimm_info *const dimm)
 		dram_print_spd_ddr3(&dimm->data);
 }
 
+/* Column address bits of the DIMMs that dimm_is_usable() left out, 0 for the others */
+static uint8_t ignored_col_bits[NUM_CHANNELS][NUM_SLOTS];
+
+static void print_ignored_dimm(uint8_t channel, uint8_t slot, uint8_t col_bits)
+{
+	printk(BIOS_ERR, "CH%uS%u: DIMM ignored, %u column address bits, Haswell has 10\n",
+	       channel, slot, col_bits);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Haswell Trad addresses DDR3 devices with 10 column address bits only:
+ * the controller is told the size, ranks and width of a DIMM, not its
+ * column bits. A DIMM of 8 Gb x8 devices (16 GiB, dual rank) has 11. It
+ * trains with good margins, then memory corrupts, and the memory test
+ * goes through the controller, which cannot see the missing column bit
+ * (https://ticket.coreboot.org/issues/626). Leave such a DIMM out. Its
+ * data is cleared, so it neither adds to the channel nor becomes DIMM A.
+ */
+static bool dimm_is_usable(struct raminit_dimm_info *const dimm, uint8_t channel, uint8_t slot)
+{
+	if (is_hsw_ult() || dimm->data.col_bits <= 10)
+		return true;
+
+	print_ignored_dimm(channel, slot, dimm->data.col_bits);
+	ignored_col_bits[channel][slot] = dimm->data.col_bits;
+	memset(&dimm->data, 0, sizeof(dimm->data));
+	dimm->valid = false;
+	return false;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Repeat the error once the console is in CBMEM. A DIMM change forces a
+ * training, whose log overflows the pre-RAM console and loses its start.
+ */
+void report_ignored_dimms(void)
+{
+	for (uint8_t channel = 0; channel < NUM_CHANNELS; channel++) {
+		for (uint8_t slot = 0; slot < NUM_SLOTS; slot++) {
+			const uint8_t col_bits = ignored_col_bits[channel][slot];
+			if (col_bits)
+				print_ignored_dimm(channel, slot, col_bits);
+		}
+	}
+}
+
 static enum raminit_status find_common_spd_parameters(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 {
 	const union pci_capid0_a_reg capid0_a = {
@@ -98,9 +143,11 @@ static enum raminit_status find_common_spd_parameters(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 	ctrl->tCWL = 0;
 	ctrl->tCMD = 0;
 	ctrl->chanmap = 0;
+	memset(ignored_col_bits, 0, sizeof(ignored_col_bits));
 
 	bool yes_ecc = false;
 	bool not_ecc = false;
+	uint8_t ignored = 0;
 
 	for (uint8_t channel = 0; channel < NUM_CHANNELS; channel++) {
 		ctrl->dpc[channel] = 0;
@@ -114,6 +161,10 @@ static enum raminit_status find_common_spd_parameters(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 
 			printk(RAM_DEBUG, "\nCH%uS%u SPD:\n", channel, slot);
 			decode_spd(dimm);
+			if (!dimm_is_usable(dimm, channel, slot)) {
+				ignored++;
+				continue;
+			}
 
 			ctrl->chanmap |= BIT(channel);
 			ctrl->dpc[channel]++;
@@ -150,6 +201,10 @@ static enum raminit_status find_common_spd_parameters(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (!ctrl->chanmap && ignored) {
+		printk(BIOS_ERR, "No usable DIMMs: all have more than 10 column bits\n");
+		return RAMINIT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED_MEMORY;
+	}
 	if (!ctrl->chanmap) {
 		printk(BIOS_ERR, "No DIMMs were found\n");
 		return RAMINIT_STATUS_NO_MEMORY_INSTALLED;
-- 
2.47.3

